    "body": "## Summary\n- persist the latest accepted signed Stripe payout `Event.created` watermark on payout requests\n- ignore strictly older terminal payout webhooks before any transfer reversal or wallet settlement can run\n- keep provider reconciliation compatible without inventing Stripe event timestamps\n- add Flyway V54, regression tests, and payout-ordering documentation\n\n## Financial safety\n- identity validation still runs before ordering decisions\n- failed/canceled payout compensation keeps the existing stable Stripe reversal idempotency key\n- the ordering watermark advances only in the same transaction as local settlement\n- equal-second contradictory terminal observations remain fail-closed rather than guessing an order\n\n## Validation\nGitHub Actions required before merge: API verify, Web verify, Production Compose contract, runtime/container smoke, and financial smoke workflows.",
